            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0668" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v16/pg628"/>

                <head>293. Letter From the Assistant Secretary of Defense for International Security
                    Affairs (Gray) to the
                    Assistant Secretary of State for Near Eastern, South Asian, and African Affairs
                        (Rountree)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d293-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                        1956</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Bill</hi>: This is to inform you that the
                    Department of Defense concurs with Contingency Papers 1 through 7, inclusive,
                    prepared pursuant to NSC Action 1593–b.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d293-f2"/></p>
                <p>While the implications of forays (or outright war) by Israel against Jordan are
                    not dealt with in any of the Contingency Papers, I am sure you will agree that
                    such actions could negate our efforts towards a peaceful solution to the Suez
                    problem. These raids, which inherently carry the threat of all out Israel-Jordan
                    hostilities, tend to unify the Arab and other Moslem States in their attitudes
                    not only toward the Arab-Israeli dispute but also with regard to the Suez
                    situation. I would therefore urge that in our representations to the Israeli
                    authorities we point out to them the adverse effects their <pb facs="0669"
                        n="629" xml:id="pg629"/> hostile actions could have upon our efforts to
                    bring about a timely and peaceful settlement of the Suez problem. Sincerely
                    yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Gordon
                            Gray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
